WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.840
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:05.110 --> 00:06.111
THIS IS A WORK OF FICTION.

3
00:06.194 --> 00:08.030
THERE IS NO RELATION TO REAL PEOPLE OR EVENTS.

4
00:09.656 --> 00:11.658
[♪ tender music playing]

5
00:13.076 --> 00:14.077
How did you get here?

6
00:14.161 --> 00:15.287
It wasn't too hard on you?

7
00:15.370 --> 00:16.371
[chuckles]

8
00:20.208 --> 00:21.209
Oh!

9
00:22.169 --> 00:23.879
These stars are beautiful.

10
00:24.630 --> 00:27.507
It gives me courage looking at them shine like this.

11
00:27.591 --> 00:29.676
Thank you for your gift, Yubin.

12
00:29.760 --> 00:30.761
Mm-hmm.

13
00:34.848 --> 00:35.849
[exclaims]

14
00:36.433 --> 00:37.601
When are you going back?

15
00:38.268 --> 00:39.394
How long can you stay?

16
00:39.478 --> 00:40.479
[Karin] Hmm?

17
00:41.063 --> 00:42.189
Hmm.

18
00:42.939 --> 00:44.775
Well, since my goal was to meet up in person…

19
00:44.858 --> 00:46.652
-Yeah? -Tomorrow, I think?

20
00:46.735 --> 00:48.028
What?

21
00:48.111 --> 00:49.738
-Tomorrow? -Oh.

22
00:49.821 --> 00:51.907
-Is that bad? -Yeah, it is, because you have to go

23
00:51.990 --> 00:53.450
-on a date with me in Korea. -Mmm.

24
00:53.533 --> 00:55.369
-Go on a date? -So you can't leave tomorrow, okay?

25
00:55.452 --> 00:57.621
-[in Korean] Come on. Let's go. -[in English] All right, all right.

26
00:57.704 --> 00:59.414
-[in English] Come on, come on. -[chuckles]

27
01:00.082 --> 01:01.625
[Yubin] What? Tomorrow?

28
01:01.708 --> 01:04.961
WINNER BEAUTIFUL HOUSE OF THE YEAR

29
01:05.045 --> 01:06.505
LEE YUBIN

30
01:06.588 --> 01:08.548
EPISODE 7

31
01:08.632 --> 01:09.633
[door lock beeping]

32
01:10.550 --> 01:12.552
-[in Korean] It's cold. Come on in. -[Karin, in English] Here?

33
01:12.636 --> 01:14.554
Ooh.

34
01:14.638 --> 01:15.639
[gasps]

35
01:17.516 --> 01:19.685
Thanks for inviting me to your house.

36
01:22.187 --> 01:24.564
[in Korean] Whoa, the heater.

37
01:25.107 --> 01:26.108
[heater beeps]

38
01:26.817 --> 01:29.903
[sighs, speaks English] It should kick on soon. It'll just be a second.

39
01:30.654 --> 01:32.447
It's all right. I don't mind.

40
01:32.531 --> 01:34.574
Oh, Karin. Hot cocoa?

41
01:34.658 --> 01:36.910
-[in Korean] Mm-hmm. I'd love that. -Ah, great.

42
01:36.993 --> 01:38.078
[Karin chuckles]

43
02:01.601 --> 02:03.728
[♪ tender music playing]

44
02:03.812 --> 02:04.813
[chuckles]

45
02:09.234 --> 02:10.235
[gasps]

46
02:21.413 --> 02:23.457
[sighs, chuckles]

47
02:38.638 --> 02:39.639
[chuckles]

48
02:42.809 --> 02:45.395
[in Korean] All right. There.

49
02:47.022 --> 02:48.190
Here you go.

50
02:48.732 --> 02:51.485
[in English] Yay, thanks. This looks so good. Wow.

51
02:53.945 --> 02:54.946
[blows]

52
02:57.491 --> 02:58.533
-Hmm. -Mmm.

53
02:58.617 --> 03:00.994
-How does it taste? -[in Korean] Perfect.

54
03:01.077 --> 03:02.454
-Perfect? -Mm-hmm. [chuckles]

55
03:02.537 --> 03:04.581
-[chuckles, in English] Oh, I'm glad. -[chuckles]

56
03:07.876 --> 03:09.252
Mmm.

57
03:10.253 --> 03:13.590
Since I've been gone, how have things been going in Japan?

58
03:14.591 --> 03:16.551
-Business as usual, I guess. -Mmm.

59
03:17.052 --> 03:21.223
Tending to the strawberries, working in the fields…

60
03:22.933 --> 03:26.269
Although, doing things alone again is pretty tough.

61
03:26.353 --> 03:27.604
It's been a while.

62
03:31.024 --> 03:32.108
You missed me, right?

63
03:37.405 --> 03:40.742
I missed the Korean toast that you used to make me every morning.

64
03:40.825 --> 03:42.244
You missed me, right?

65
03:42.327 --> 03:45.205
-Your Korean toast is what I missed. -That's not what I asked.

66
03:45.288 --> 03:47.624
-Hmm? -Did you miss me or not? Hmm?

67
03:48.208 --> 03:49.209
[chuckling]

68
03:49.292 --> 03:51.169
You didn't miss me at all?

69
03:51.878 --> 03:53.004
Yes, I missed you too.

70
03:53.088 --> 03:55.257
You're too late. You're too late. You're too late.

71
03:55.340 --> 03:56.883
-Too late? -[in Korean] Too late!

72
03:56.967 --> 03:59.469
[in English] You took too long! Did you miss me?

73
03:59.553 --> 04:00.929
I missed you very much.

74
04:01.012 --> 04:02.347
A lot more than I can say.

75
04:02.430 --> 04:04.933
-You aren't lying? -Of course not.

76
04:05.016 --> 04:07.269
-Hmm. -And you, Yubin?

77
04:07.352 --> 04:08.728
Oh, me as well.

78
04:08.812 --> 04:11.189
I've also missed the Korean toast that I made.

79
04:11.898 --> 04:13.191
-What? -Huh?

80
04:13.692 --> 04:14.985
-[chuckles] -[chuckles]

81
04:15.068 --> 04:16.528
I missed you too, all right?

82
04:16.611 --> 04:17.862
[both laugh]

83
04:17.946 --> 04:19.322
-Lucky me. -Lucky me.

84
04:19.406 --> 04:20.448
[Yubin laughs]

85
04:21.366 --> 04:23.285
-[Karin] That thing is so pretty. -Wow. Pretty.

86
04:23.368 --> 04:24.786
-Mmm. -Mm-hmm.

87
04:25.662 --> 04:27.163
That "thing" is a whale.

88
04:27.247 --> 04:29.958
-Yeah, that thing is pretty. -Yeah. That "thing."

89
04:30.041 --> 04:32.127
-What? -It's not "pretty."

90
04:32.711 --> 04:34.921
-That's not pretty? -Not "pretty." "Whale."

91
04:35.672 --> 04:36.673
Huh?

92
04:36.756 --> 04:38.300
-You're saying it's "pretty?" -Mmm.

93
04:38.383 --> 04:39.426
It's a whale.

94
04:39.509 --> 04:41.136
[both laugh]

95
04:41.219 --> 04:42.470
Oh, wait. Do you mean in Korean?

96
04:42.554 --> 04:44.264
-Yeah, in Korean. "That thing." -"That thing."

97
04:44.347 --> 04:45.348
-It means… -It means

98
04:45.432 --> 04:46.808
-a whale. Yeah. -…a whale?

99
04:46.892 --> 04:48.560
-What? -Those words sound alike.

100
04:48.643 --> 04:49.811
-Oh, really? -Mm-hmm.

101
04:49.895 --> 04:53.356
-No way. "Whale" is the same word? -Yeah, "that thing" means "whale."

102
04:53.440 --> 04:55.442
-[laughing] -Ah. [laughing]

103
04:57.777 --> 04:59.321
-The second time was… -Mm-hmm.

104
04:59.863 --> 05:02.032
-…the other day, I think? -Oh. Oh, yeah?

105
05:04.326 --> 05:06.411
[Karin] Lucky me, lucky me.

106
05:08.246 --> 05:10.832
Everybody on Charo Island are doing well.

107
05:11.917 --> 05:13.752
[gasps] Right! Grandma Hana…

108
05:16.463 --> 05:17.505
Hmm?

109
05:17.589 --> 05:19.341
[chuckles softly]

110
05:20.216 --> 05:21.343
Sleeping?

111
05:22.886 --> 05:23.887
[chuckles]

112
05:34.314 --> 05:35.732
Good night, Yubin.

113
06:31.037 --> 06:32.539
[moans]

114
06:37.752 --> 06:38.753
Yubin.

115
06:40.964 --> 06:42.132
Karin.

116
06:43.049 --> 06:44.050
[Karin] Mmm.

117
06:45.927 --> 06:46.928
[Yubin] Hmm?

118
06:52.600 --> 06:54.310
Will you be my girlfriend?

119
06:56.688 --> 06:58.273
[Karin] Mmm. Mm-hmm.

120
06:59.274 --> 07:00.275
[Yubin] Mm-hmm?

121
07:08.366 --> 07:10.493
-Hmm? -[Karin] Hmm?

122
07:10.577 --> 07:11.786
Hmm?

123
07:13.621 --> 07:15.081
-Huh? -Huh?

124
07:16.791 --> 07:18.918
Wait. What did you say?

125
07:19.002 --> 07:21.588
What… What did I just say?

126
07:21.671 --> 07:24.799
I asked if you would be my girlfriend.

127
07:28.511 --> 07:29.512
[stammers]

128
07:31.431 --> 07:32.599
[clears throat]

129
07:33.808 --> 07:34.809
Yes.

130
07:34.893 --> 07:37.228
-[sighs, laughing] -[laughing]

131
07:37.896 --> 07:40.440
I'm really looking forward to being your girlfriend.

132
07:42.150 --> 07:43.568
-[chuckles] -[Yubin grunts]

133
07:44.110 --> 07:46.571
I'm really looking forward to being your boyfriend.

134
07:46.654 --> 07:48.198
-You mean it? -Yeah.

135
07:51.743 --> 07:52.952
Ask me again.

136
07:54.370 --> 07:56.790
-Will you be my girlfriend? -[giggling]

137
08:00.627 --> 08:03.004
-[squeals, laughing] -[laughing]

138
08:04.547 --> 08:06.966
-[Yubin] This river is called Hangang. -[Karin] Mm-hmm?

139
08:07.592 --> 08:08.802
-Hangang? -Uh-huh.

140
08:08.885 --> 08:10.470
-I've seen photos of it. -Mmm.

141
08:12.347 --> 08:13.556
[in Korean] I'm hungry.

142
08:14.098 --> 08:15.391
-You're hungry? -Mm-hmm.

143
08:15.475 --> 08:16.476
Uh…

144
08:17.185 --> 08:20.188
-[in English] What do you want to eat? -Hmm…

145
08:21.105 --> 08:22.273
Tteokbokki!

146
08:22.357 --> 08:24.108
-Tteokbokki? -Yeah. I want that.

147
08:24.192 --> 08:25.401
-The spicy kind. -Tteokbokki?

148
08:25.485 --> 08:27.862
-What's wrong with that? -[sighs, speaks Korean] It's pretty spicy.

149
08:28.988 --> 08:30.824
-[Yubin] All right. -[Karin, in English] Wow.

150
08:30.907 --> 08:32.700
[Yubin, in Korean] Thank you.

151
08:36.788 --> 08:38.790
-Mmm. -[in English] Is it okay?

152
08:38.873 --> 08:40.041
[in Korean] How is it?

153
08:40.124 --> 08:41.417
[in English] Is it hot?

154
08:41.501 --> 08:44.546
-[in Korean] Is it spicy? It is, isn't it? -[in English] Yeah, it's so spicy. [yelps]

155
08:45.130 --> 08:47.090
-[groans] -[in Korean] Here.

156
08:47.173 --> 08:48.174
JJEONGIGA TTEOKBOKKI

157
08:48.258 --> 08:49.300
[Karin, in English] So spicy!

158
08:50.927 --> 08:52.220
-Hot. [grunts] -[Yubin chuckles]

159
08:52.303 --> 08:53.304
Is it all right?

160
08:53.388 --> 08:54.848
-Mmm. It's so good. -Mm-hmm.

161
08:54.931 --> 08:56.099
-Is it good? -Mm-hmm.

162
08:56.182 --> 08:57.517
[Yubin, in Korean] Check this out.

163
08:58.810 --> 09:00.103
[in English] Thank you.

164
09:00.186 --> 09:02.230
-[in Korean] You go like this… -Mmm.

165
09:02.313 --> 09:03.940
-[in English] How is it? -Mmm.

166
09:04.524 --> 09:06.317
-It's good. -Mmm.

167
09:06.401 --> 09:08.111
-[in Korean] It's good. -It's good? You like it, right?

168
09:08.194 --> 09:10.572
-[in English] Now that we're full of food… -Mm-hmm.

169
09:10.655 --> 09:11.865
…it's time to work it off.

170
09:11.948 --> 09:14.075
-[sucks teeth] All right. Whoever wins… -Yeah. Uh-huh.

171
09:14.159 --> 09:15.660
…gets their wish granted by the loser.

172
09:15.743 --> 09:17.245
-Okay. [in Korean] Let's go! -[in English] Okay?

173
09:17.328 --> 09:19.330
[♪ upbeat music playing]

174
09:23.293 --> 09:24.294
Whoa!

175
09:26.171 --> 09:27.172
-Whoa. -[Karin chuckles]

176
09:37.807 --> 09:38.892
[sighs]

177
09:40.351 --> 09:41.769
[Karin] Time's up.

178
09:41.853 --> 09:43.479
[in Korean] How are you so good at this?

179
09:54.365 --> 09:55.366
Ready?

180
09:57.452 --> 09:58.953
[Yubin] Whoa, whoa. Oh!

181
09:59.954 --> 10:01.331
-[chuckles] -[exclaims]

182
10:01.414 --> 10:03.958
-[air hockey table chimes] -[in English] Okay!

183
10:05.293 --> 10:07.045
Yay! [giggling]

184
10:07.128 --> 10:08.755
Yeah! Yeah! [laughs]

185
10:09.464 --> 10:11.299
-[air hockey table chimes] -Yeah!

186
10:12.842 --> 10:14.427
[sucks teeth] Let's see.

187
10:14.510 --> 10:18.556
Since you're the winner, I guess you get to make a wish.

188
10:18.640 --> 10:19.641
-I get the wish? -Go ahead.

189
10:19.724 --> 10:20.934
-Okay. -What is it?

190
10:21.726 --> 10:23.478
Hmm. What do I wish?

191
10:23.561 --> 10:25.563
Let me think…

192
10:25.647 --> 10:26.648
[Yubin] Mmm.

193
10:27.440 --> 10:28.775
That, over there.

194
10:28.858 --> 10:30.401
-Let's go in there. -Huh? That store?

195
10:30.485 --> 10:32.028
-Yeah, that one. -Oh, all right.

196
10:33.821 --> 10:34.822
[gasps]

197
10:34.906 --> 10:36.157
Look at this!

198
10:38.743 --> 10:39.744
-Oh, it's cute. -Oh, wow.

199
10:39.827 --> 10:41.246
-Yeah, it's cute. -Mmm.

200
10:41.871 --> 10:44.165
-Oh! -[Karin] Oh.

201
10:44.249 --> 10:45.917
-It's a bug. -That's a caterpillar.

202
10:46.000 --> 10:48.253
-Uh-huh. -[in Korean] Aw, it's so cute! [chuckles]

203
10:48.336 --> 10:49.629
-[in English] Wait. -Huh?

204
10:49.712 --> 10:51.923
-[elongated] Oh. -What?

205
10:52.006 --> 10:53.007
Spitting image.

206
10:53.091 --> 10:55.051
-That thing? -It's your twin. [laughing]

207
10:55.134 --> 10:57.345
[in Korean] What'd you say? [scoffs, chuckles]

208
10:57.428 --> 10:59.430
-[in English] Yeah. You look alike. -We do not!

209
11:00.306 --> 11:01.599
What the heck?

210
11:02.600 --> 11:04.978
[in Korean] Let's get these two.

211
11:05.061 --> 11:06.062
-Mm-hmm. -All right.

212
11:06.145 --> 11:07.689
-[in English] Ah. Wait a sec. -Hmm?

213
11:12.068 --> 11:13.569
Let's match, okay?

214
11:13.653 --> 11:14.654
Mmm.

215
11:14.737 --> 11:16.322
I've always wanted to try this…

216
11:16.406 --> 11:17.699
[in Korean] …with a boyfriend.

217
11:18.449 --> 11:21.119
-[in English] We're a couple? -Mm-hmm. We're a couple.

218
11:21.202 --> 11:24.914
Okay, from now on, we'll be known as "the bug couple."

219
11:24.998 --> 11:26.541
-"The bug couple"? -Yeah.

220
11:26.624 --> 11:27.625
No, thanks.

221
11:27.709 --> 11:29.294
We're "the ttalgi couple." Strawberry couple.

222
11:29.377 --> 11:30.461
[singsongy] Mm-mmm.

223
11:30.545 --> 11:32.338
-Bugs. Bugs are much cuter. -[in Korean] Strawberry.

224
11:32.422 --> 11:33.423
[in English] I wanna be "the bug couple."

225
11:33.506 --> 11:35.675
-Strawberries are way cuter though. -Mm-mmm, mm-mmm.

226
11:35.758 --> 11:38.303
-Bugs, bugs, bugs. -Hey, not "the bug couple."

227
11:39.762 --> 11:41.681
[electronic voice, in Korean] Two, one…

228
11:41.764 --> 11:42.765
[camera shuttering]

229
11:49.480 --> 11:50.523
[in English] It's ready.

230
11:50.606 --> 11:51.941
Ah, ramyeon.

231
11:52.025 --> 11:53.776
Here. [hums]

232
11:53.860 --> 11:55.361
-[exclaims] -[chuckles]

233
11:55.445 --> 11:58.239
-I saw Hangang River ramyeon online. -Mmm.

234
11:58.990 --> 11:59.991
It's time to eat.

235
12:00.074 --> 12:01.617
-[in Korean] Let's dig in. -Okay.

236
12:07.999 --> 12:09.500
-[in English] Well? -Mmm. Mmm!

237
12:09.584 --> 12:11.127
-You like it? -[in Korean] Mm-hmm. So good!

238
12:11.210 --> 12:12.378
Mmm.

239
12:17.592 --> 12:18.718
[in English] Is it done?

240
12:21.804 --> 12:23.097
-[Yubin sighs] -[chuckles]

241
12:23.181 --> 12:24.307
Thank you.

242
12:24.390 --> 12:25.391
Mmm.

243
12:26.434 --> 12:28.186
Yubin, I had so much fun today.

244
12:28.269 --> 12:31.606
Ah, I'm so glad. It was a great day, wasn't it?

245
12:31.689 --> 12:32.815
-It really was. -Mm-hmm.

246
12:32.899 --> 12:34.817
What about tomorrow?

247
12:34.901 --> 12:36.819
Is there anywhere you have in mind?

248
12:36.903 --> 12:38.821
Uh, anywhere?

249
12:38.905 --> 12:40.490
Mm-hmm. Anywhere.

250
12:41.991 --> 12:44.619
Um… [exhales sharply]

251
12:49.040 --> 12:50.208
Uh…

252
12:51.751 --> 12:52.794
Mm-hmm.

253
12:54.420 --> 12:55.671
There is.

254
13:14.273 --> 13:15.316
Here we are.

255
13:17.985 --> 13:20.738
THE TREE OF LEE GYEONGSU

256
13:22.240 --> 13:24.659
"Lee Gyeongsu."

257
13:28.079 --> 13:29.205
Mm-hmm.

258
13:30.498 --> 13:32.750
Lee Gyeongsu… he was my dad.

259
13:37.463 --> 13:39.757
[♪ gentle piano music playing]

260
13:39.841 --> 13:40.842
Really?

261
13:40.925 --> 13:41.926
Mm-hmm.

262
13:42.927 --> 13:44.428
Lee Gyeongsu was your dad?

263
13:44.512 --> 13:45.513
Mm-hmm.

264
13:54.981 --> 13:55.982
Then…

265
13:58.234 --> 14:00.319
that figurine I've been keeping safe…

266
14:06.701 --> 14:07.702
[sighs]

267
14:12.748 --> 14:13.749
Now I get it.

268
14:23.176 --> 14:24.635
[in Korean] Long time no see.

269
14:26.470 --> 14:28.097
[in English] …Mr. Gyeongsu, sir.

270
14:30.641 --> 14:31.809
[in Korean] It's been a while,

271
14:33.477 --> 14:34.562
Father.

272
14:36.939 --> 14:37.940
Dad.

273
14:38.024 --> 14:39.066
Yeah?

274
14:39.817 --> 14:42.195
Don't you ever get tired of studying like that all the time?

275
14:42.278 --> 14:43.279
STRAWBERRY

276
14:44.530 --> 14:45.698
Of course I do.

277
14:46.866 --> 14:48.451
But I enjoy it.

278
14:50.161 --> 14:52.914
It's hard, but you enjoy it?

279
14:52.997 --> 14:56.167
What do you enjoy doing, Yubin?

280
14:57.960 --> 14:59.795
You like drawing.

281
15:00.421 --> 15:02.089
You're good with your hands, just like your mom.

282
15:02.173 --> 15:03.174
[scoffs]

283
15:04.008 --> 15:06.552
Mine are just doodling.

284
15:16.479 --> 15:18.814
Did you draw this?

285
15:18.898 --> 15:23.569
-Give it back! -Wow, that is amazing.

286
15:26.530 --> 15:29.659
We should build our house like this someday.

287
15:33.537 --> 15:35.706
It'd be perfect if there was a tree here.

288
15:36.624 --> 15:38.751
I could sit in its shade and read a book with your mom.

289
15:39.585 --> 15:42.964
[scoffs] We don't need a tree.

290
15:43.547 --> 15:45.007
-I'll draw one myself. -Huh?

291
15:45.091 --> 15:49.262
-Wait. Hey. Let me do it. -What? I can do it.

292
15:49.345 --> 15:50.888
I know how to draw too!

293
15:50.972 --> 15:52.098
You're going to ruin it.

294
15:52.974 --> 15:54.475
Draw it over here then.

295
15:56.560 --> 15:57.561
What kind of tree do you want?

296
15:58.229 --> 16:00.147
Hmm? A big,

297
16:01.190 --> 16:02.233
nice tree.

298
16:04.694 --> 16:05.987
A long-living tree.

299
16:11.867 --> 16:14.328
Like a huge 100-year-old tree.

300
16:15.621 --> 16:18.749
[inhales sharply, chuckles] You sketched that so fast.

301
16:20.751 --> 16:22.253
It's incredible.

302
16:24.255 --> 16:26.632
The room under the tree is mine.

303
16:26.716 --> 16:28.551
No, this one's for Mom.

304
16:29.176 --> 16:31.429
Yours is this one.

305
16:31.929 --> 16:33.931
-[chuckles] Bring Mom here. -[chuckles]

306
16:34.015 --> 16:37.268
[Gyeongsu] Mom and I will share the room. [chuckles]

307
17:05.379 --> 17:06.589
[Yubin] All done.

308
17:12.303 --> 17:13.304
Ooh.

309
17:14.305 --> 17:16.265
[in English] I didn't realize I was this hungry.

310
17:16.891 --> 17:19.268
-Ooh. That looks fantastic. -[chuckles] Mmm.

311
17:19.894 --> 17:21.896
-It's doenjang jjigae. -Doenjang jjigae?

312
17:21.979 --> 17:23.189
-[Yubin] Right. -Yum.

313
17:24.774 --> 17:26.025
[sighs]

314
17:26.108 --> 17:28.027
-[phone buzzing] -[Karin] Hmm?

315
17:28.110 --> 17:30.821
MR. KUROKAWA

316
17:32.031 --> 17:34.659
Sorry, Yubin. This will only take a minute.

317
17:34.742 --> 17:35.743
Sure.

318
17:42.375 --> 17:45.169
[whispers] Okay, okay, okay.

319
17:47.088 --> 17:48.214
Karin speaking.

320
17:48.297 --> 17:49.924
Oh, Karin, hi.

321
17:50.007 --> 17:53.469
I'm checking in to see if you've thought about our talk from the other day.

322
17:55.179 --> 17:56.180
Uh…

323
17:57.223 --> 18:01.644
If you remember, I proposed we distribute your berries nationwide.

324
18:02.228 --> 18:04.647
Right. It's, uh…

325
18:06.357 --> 18:10.069
It's just… I'm not sure if the quality'd be maintainable.

326
18:10.611 --> 18:15.950
That's a large number of strawberries to be growing like that in my open field.

327
18:16.033 --> 18:17.535
I'm a little worried about it.

328
18:21.664 --> 18:24.375
With Green Nova Corporation's cutting-edge technology,

329
18:24.458 --> 18:27.586
we'll definitely be able to ensure some degree of quality.

330
18:29.046 --> 18:31.424
Some degree of quality?

331
18:31.507 --> 18:32.508
Right.

332
18:33.968 --> 18:37.888
You know I understand your dedication to preserving top-notch quality.

333
18:38.514 --> 18:42.143
However, remember that choosing one thing

334
18:42.226 --> 18:46.272
often means that another thing will inevitably fall to the wayside.

335
18:46.856 --> 18:47.940
Right.

336
18:48.023 --> 18:50.943
But listen, there's nothing for you to worry about

337
18:51.026 --> 18:54.113
with those wonderful strawberries that you've developed.

338
18:54.196 --> 18:57.116
How about I email you the proposal, for now?

339
18:57.700 --> 19:01.120
Or if you prefer, we can chat at Green Nova Corporation's office

340
19:01.203 --> 19:02.747
in the coming few days.

341
19:06.167 --> 19:07.793
All right. [sighs]

342
19:10.004 --> 19:11.338
I appreciate the offer.

343
19:12.757 --> 19:14.759
I'll reach out in the next few days.

344
19:17.219 --> 19:18.304
I will.

345
19:19.305 --> 19:20.598
Have a good night, sir.

346
19:33.194 --> 19:34.278
[sighs]

347
19:44.079 --> 19:45.581
Uh, Yubin?

348
19:49.460 --> 19:50.461
Yubin?

349
19:51.378 --> 19:52.880
-[Yubin] Ta-da! -Oh.

350
19:52.963 --> 19:55.341
[chuckles] It's your birthday celebration.

351
19:56.926 --> 19:58.302
What? [chuckles]

352
19:59.053 --> 20:00.888
-[in Korean] All right. -[chuckles]

353
20:00.971 --> 20:03.599
Come on, over here. Right this way.

354
20:03.682 --> 20:04.725
[Karin chuckles]

355
20:05.518 --> 20:06.644
[in English] Wow.

356
20:06.727 --> 20:08.604
KARIN HAPPY BIRTHDAY

357
20:08.687 --> 20:11.732
[in Korean] Ah, here you go. Put this on.

358
20:12.566 --> 20:14.109
Ah, there.

359
20:14.735 --> 20:15.778
[chuckles]

360
20:16.278 --> 20:17.530
[in English] Make a wish. Blow out the candles.

361
20:17.613 --> 20:19.490
-It's wish time? Hmm. -Put your hands like this.

362
20:28.082 --> 20:29.250
[Karin chuckles]

363
20:29.959 --> 20:31.919
-[in Korean] Thank you so much. -[chuckles]

364
20:32.002 --> 20:33.379
[in English] Thanks for being born.

365
20:37.049 --> 20:38.342
-Let's have some cake. -Okay.

366
20:40.511 --> 20:42.513
-Wow, these are cute. -Oh, they're cute?

367
20:42.596 --> 20:44.390
-They're adorable. -Which do you like more?

368
20:44.473 --> 20:45.641
-Which one? -What? All of 'em.

369
20:45.724 --> 20:47.560
-You like them all? Oh. -This one, this one, this one.

370
20:47.643 --> 20:48.936
-Want a bite? -No, thanks.

371
20:52.940 --> 20:53.941
[in Korean] Here you go…

372
20:54.024 --> 20:56.569
-[in English] Thank you, sir. -[grunts]

373
21:05.077 --> 21:07.079
[♪ tender music playing]

374
21:13.919 --> 21:15.963
Is there something on your mind?

375
21:16.046 --> 21:17.047
[Karin] Hmm?

376
21:19.550 --> 21:20.551
Hmm…

377
21:24.471 --> 21:25.639
I think that…

378
21:27.600 --> 21:30.144
I should head back to Japan tomorrow.

379
21:34.773 --> 21:37.568
[Yubin inhales deeply, sighs]

380
21:40.821 --> 21:41.947
I get it.

381
21:47.620 --> 21:50.289
I would love to stay here with you a little longer,

382
21:52.750 --> 21:55.127
but I need to take care of my strawberries.

383
21:56.962 --> 21:58.464
I came here spontaneously.

384
21:59.673 --> 22:01.091
Well, when you get back,

385
22:01.967 --> 22:05.721
will you promise you'll think about me a lot?

386
22:09.058 --> 22:10.142
Mm-hmm.

387
22:10.225 --> 22:11.769
-Oh, will you? -Mm-hmm.

388
22:11.852 --> 22:14.188
Of course I will. I'll think about you.

389
22:15.564 --> 22:16.565
[chuckles]

390
22:20.819 --> 22:22.780
-[chuckles] -[sighs]

391
22:27.034 --> 22:28.035
[Karin sighs]

392
22:31.163 --> 22:34.500
KUROKAWA

393
22:44.593 --> 22:47.930
-[footsteps approaching] -[secretary] Excuse me, Director.

394
22:48.555 --> 22:49.556
Yes?

395
22:51.767 --> 22:52.768
Director,

396
22:53.268 --> 22:56.146
I've brought additional samples of Shirahama Karin's strawberries

397
22:56.230 --> 22:57.564
-as you requested. -Ah.

398
22:57.648 --> 22:59.733
Hurry. Measure the strawberry samples' sweetness.

399
22:59.817 --> 23:00.818
Yes, sir.

400
23:03.612 --> 23:05.155
[♪ quirky music playing]

401
23:05.239 --> 23:06.240
[sucks teeth]

402
23:07.199 --> 23:08.200
Hmm…

403
23:10.953 --> 23:13.122
-Ugh. Never mind. Move aside. -[gasps]

404
23:52.536 --> 23:53.871
[beeps]

405
23:57.666 --> 23:59.752
Oh, their sweetness has evolved.

406
24:00.878 --> 24:02.421
With its quality,

407
24:02.504 --> 24:04.048
the strawberries can hold their own

408
24:04.131 --> 24:06.550
amongst Green Nova Corporation's popular products.

409
24:06.633 --> 24:08.135
In the premium lineup, no doubt.

410
24:14.141 --> 24:17.352
This variety could be the future of our company.

411
24:28.489 --> 24:29.823
[sighs heavily]

412
24:30.574 --> 24:33.494
[Mari] Karin is gone and Yubin is gone…

413
24:37.122 --> 24:38.373
And Kunam is gone too.

414
24:40.459 --> 24:41.960
[phone buzzes]

415
24:45.839 --> 24:47.132
[Karin] I'm at the airport.

416
24:48.175 --> 24:49.176
[sighs]

417
24:50.469 --> 24:52.054
Looks like she made it back all right.

418
24:57.684 --> 25:00.187
[♪ mystical music plays]

419
25:07.986 --> 25:08.987
[sighs]

420
25:20.624 --> 25:21.875
Tell me, cards…

421
25:23.544 --> 25:25.546
what does fate have in store for us?

422
25:27.381 --> 25:28.507
[sighs]

423
25:55.450 --> 25:57.202
[exhales deeply]

424
26:01.039 --> 26:03.458
[thunderclap, rumbling]

425
26:04.168 --> 26:05.377
Does this mean…

426
26:06.336 --> 26:08.046
a crumbling heart?

427
26:09.173 --> 26:11.383
[♪ suspenseful music plays]

428
26:15.470 --> 26:16.471
[gasps]

429
26:16.555 --> 26:17.556
[sinister laugh]

430
26:17.639 --> 26:19.725
Could this mean "temptation"?

431
26:19.808 --> 26:23.061
No way. Is Kunam seeing another woman?

432
26:36.450 --> 26:38.035
[♪ ominous music playing]

433
26:38.118 --> 26:39.369
[gasps]

434
26:40.662 --> 26:43.040
-[swords clanking] -[gasps, whimpers]

435
26:43.123 --> 26:44.708
Anything but that!

436
26:44.791 --> 26:46.960
Dear tarot cards, this can't be my destiny!

437
26:47.044 --> 26:50.964
Oh, please, please change your mind! [sobs]

438
26:51.048 --> 26:52.382
-[vehicle approaching] -[gasps]

439
26:52.466 --> 26:53.842
-Kunam? -[engine shuts off]

440
26:59.514 --> 27:00.849
[sighs]

441
27:00.933 --> 27:02.935
Oh. Hi, Mari.

442
27:04.144 --> 27:06.605
-Hi, Grandpa Asahi. -It's nice to see you.

443
27:15.322 --> 27:16.782
-Are you looking for something? -Ah.

444
27:16.865 --> 27:18.617
Uh… It's… right here.

445
27:18.700 --> 27:20.661
-Curry powder. I ran out earlier. -Oh!

446
27:20.744 --> 27:21.745
[both chuckle]

447
27:21.828 --> 27:23.455
I'll ring you up over here.

448
27:30.963 --> 27:32.130
[register beeping]

449
27:34.049 --> 27:38.136
Grandpa Asahi, you've haven't seen Kunam around lately, have you?

450
27:39.554 --> 27:41.473
-Has it been a while? -Yeah.

451
27:42.015 --> 27:43.934
Well, he's been pretty busy, you know.

452
27:44.017 --> 27:45.435
[scoffs]

453
27:45.519 --> 27:47.312
Oh, yeah? What's he been so busy with?

454
27:47.396 --> 27:49.314
Chasing after a bunch of women?

455
27:49.398 --> 27:51.316
Mari, he's got you, right?

456
27:51.400 --> 27:53.568
He's not chasing other girls.

457
27:53.652 --> 27:57.406
Well, what he told me is that he's been job-hunting.

458
27:57.489 --> 27:58.782
What?

459
27:58.865 --> 28:01.410
Wait, I thought he was happy working here. Wasn't he?

460
28:01.493 --> 28:06.331
Yes, but he said that just working here doesn't qualify towards a work visa.

461
28:07.290 --> 28:09.626
That's why he's been busy pounding the pavement,

462
28:09.710 --> 28:11.461
looking for qualifying employment.

463
28:12.170 --> 28:13.964
[Kunam] Sorry to do this out of the blue.

464
28:14.047 --> 28:15.716
Ah, no, I understand.

465
28:16.550 --> 28:17.801
Go on.

466
28:17.884 --> 28:21.054
I think that we should take a break.

467
28:21.138 --> 28:22.514
[exclaims]

468
28:26.059 --> 28:27.060
What the heck?

469
28:27.144 --> 28:30.397
He always shows up no matter what, even if I tell him not to come here.

470
28:30.480 --> 28:32.816
He can't even bother to say hi?

471
28:35.360 --> 28:37.946
It's all beginning to make sense now.

472
28:38.780 --> 28:41.616
[Asahi] He came to Charo Island to visit and explore,

473
28:41.700 --> 28:44.453
but then he ended up staying here.

474
28:44.536 --> 28:45.704
It must've caught up to him

475
28:45.787 --> 28:48.623
because he didn't think to prepare for a work visa.

476
28:49.624 --> 28:53.378
Uh, excuse me… I think that I'm a little lost.

477
28:53.879 --> 28:57.132
Do you happen to know where I can find the ferry terminal?

478
28:57.716 --> 28:58.884
It's that way.

479
29:00.135 --> 29:02.429
But you'll never make it before they leave the port.

480
29:02.512 --> 29:04.806
Then, when will the next ferry arrive?

481
29:04.890 --> 29:06.266
Not for another two hours.

482
29:06.349 --> 29:07.684
Two hours…

483
29:08.310 --> 29:09.311
[groans]

484
29:09.895 --> 29:11.438
-[sighs] -[chuckles]

485
29:11.521 --> 29:12.939
[♪ whimsical music playing]

486
29:13.857 --> 29:15.192
Do you wanna sit down?

487
29:15.901 --> 29:16.902
[in Korean] Sorry?

488
29:16.985 --> 29:18.987
[in English] Your legs look tired from walking around.

489
29:21.948 --> 29:22.949
Thanks.

490
29:26.244 --> 29:27.245
[Mari] Mmm.

491
29:30.415 --> 29:31.750
Oh, thank you so much.

492
29:35.712 --> 29:40.258
As a tourist or traveler or whatever, you're just wandering around anyway.

493
29:40.926 --> 29:43.845
You don't need to be so precious about sticking to a schedule.

494
29:43.929 --> 29:45.931
[♪ music continues]

495
29:54.523 --> 29:55.524
[Kunam, in Korean] Wow…

496
29:57.109 --> 29:58.693
[chuckles]

497
30:02.781 --> 30:06.451
[in English] This seat right here has the best view on Charo island.

498
30:16.503 --> 30:18.255
Um, could…

499
30:18.338 --> 30:20.382
I stay here…

500
30:20.465 --> 30:22.884
uh, a little while longer?

501
30:23.677 --> 30:25.345
Not just for two hours?

502
30:25.428 --> 30:26.596
[chuckles]

503
30:27.389 --> 30:30.058
Do what you want. Why are you asking me?

504
30:30.142 --> 30:32.269
Don't cause trouble while you're here, all right?

505
30:41.111 --> 30:42.612
Good morning!

506
30:48.034 --> 30:49.411
[in Korean] All right.

507
30:53.748 --> 30:57.294
[in English] Um, I just started working over there! Right over there.

508
30:57.377 --> 30:58.378
[chuckles]

509
30:58.962 --> 31:01.047
Don't cause any trouble, got it?

510
31:01.631 --> 31:02.883
Uh, one more thing.

511
31:03.508 --> 31:06.261
My name is Park Kunam.

512
31:08.513 --> 31:11.224
It's nice to meet you, then. I'm Mizuno Mari.

513
31:11.308 --> 31:12.475
Mari…

514
31:13.143 --> 31:14.311
Mizuno Mari…

515
31:15.770 --> 31:18.273
Mari, I'm so happy to meet you.

516
31:18.356 --> 31:20.358
[♪ sentimental music playing]

517
31:27.407 --> 31:28.408
[music ends]

518
31:31.036 --> 31:33.038
[alarm beeping]

519
31:35.749 --> 31:37.209
-[groans] -[phone chimes]

520
31:42.172 --> 31:43.715
[Yubin, in Korean] Good morning, Karin.

521
31:43.798 --> 31:45.550
I just got up.

522
31:45.634 --> 31:46.885
[in English] Morning.

523
31:46.968 --> 31:49.846
[♪ whimsical music playing]

524
31:53.516 --> 31:56.061
Good morning, Yubin. You're an early bird.

525
31:56.144 --> 31:57.145
[Yubin, in Korean] Yeah.

526
31:58.897 --> 32:01.274
-[Karin, in English] What are you doing? -[in Korean] Just zoning out.

527
32:01.942 --> 32:03.276
[chuckles]

528
32:05.320 --> 32:07.906
-[phone buzzes] -Which should I go with?

529
32:09.532 --> 32:11.534
This one?

530
32:14.579 --> 32:15.580
Or this one?

531
32:20.043 --> 32:21.044
[shutter clicks]

532
32:23.672 --> 32:24.673
[shutter clicks]

533
32:24.756 --> 32:27.050
-[phone chimes] -[Karin] Hmm?

534
32:30.512 --> 32:31.888
[Yubin] Which do you like better?

535
32:33.348 --> 32:34.599
[Karin] Hmm.

536
32:39.396 --> 32:42.440
[in English] Hmm… I like the first one!

537
32:44.484 --> 32:47.153
[in Korean] The first one. Okay.

538
32:49.155 --> 32:50.699
[food sizzling]

539
32:52.701 --> 32:55.578
[in English] Hot, hot… ugh. [yelps]

540
32:57.789 --> 32:59.332
Did I make it right?

541
32:59.416 --> 33:03.962
It kind of looks different from the toast you made before…

542
33:04.045 --> 33:05.046
[phone buzzes]

543
33:05.547 --> 33:06.673
[Yubin] Hmm.

544
33:06.756 --> 33:07.757
[Karin] Did I make it right?

545
33:07.841 --> 33:10.093
It kind of looks different from the toast you made before…

546
33:10.176 --> 33:15.515
[in Korean] You can be more generous with the sugar.

547
33:16.099 --> 33:18.351
You can be more generous with the sugar.

548
33:19.644 --> 33:21.104
[in English] More generous?

549
33:21.980 --> 33:23.064
How much should I add?

550
33:24.024 --> 33:28.611
[in Korean] As much as you miss me.

551
33:29.863 --> 33:31.573
As much as you miss me.

552
33:31.656 --> 33:32.657
[Karin chortles]

553
33:33.325 --> 33:35.327
[♪ whimsical music continues]

554
33:44.669 --> 33:45.879
[sighing] Ah…

555
33:45.962 --> 33:47.380
She misses me a lot.

556
33:56.931 --> 33:57.932
[music ends]

557
34:03.730 --> 34:05.815
[pages flipping]

558
34:16.993 --> 34:19.329
-[clipboard thuds] -[sighs]

559
34:35.136 --> 34:39.516
Which team manages the bio-based building materials?

560
34:41.726 --> 34:43.395
I need an explanation.

561
34:44.479 --> 34:48.483
You got residents to sign consent forms before the project even kicked off.

562
34:49.401 --> 34:51.820
Most of them are elderly residents too.

563
34:51.903 --> 34:56.783
[chuckles] Mr. Lee, I wish you'd see the bigger picture here.

564
34:56.866 --> 34:58.952
It's better to clear off some farmland

565
34:59.035 --> 35:02.747
if it means revitalizing the whole village.

566
35:03.373 --> 35:04.624
Besides,

567
35:05.375 --> 35:08.211
we'll pay a generous compensation to the residents.

568
35:08.294 --> 35:09.462
Compensation?

569
35:10.588 --> 35:14.342
It's not just some land.

570
35:14.426 --> 35:16.803
It's the residents' way of life.

571
35:16.886 --> 35:19.639
How many times do I have to tell you

572
35:19.723 --> 35:21.891
that profit is the company's greatest priority?

573
35:21.975 --> 35:25.562
Yes, profit is important.

574
35:26.479 --> 35:29.691
You've reported an estimated profit margin of 12%.

575
35:29.774 --> 35:32.736
I looked into the risk factors.

576
35:32.819 --> 35:37.198
A 40% risk of delay due to the farmland's rezoning denial.

577
35:37.741 --> 35:42.787
15% loss from potential class action suit if the consent is found to be forged.

578
35:42.871 --> 35:47.292
The company's image would take a hit if it is deemed an environmental issue.

579
35:47.375 --> 35:51.045
There would be a 20% drop in presale premium.

580
35:51.129 --> 35:52.839
What do you think about that?

581
35:53.590 --> 35:54.966
That was the best-case scenario…

582
35:55.049 --> 35:56.843
And the worst case?

583
35:57.343 --> 35:58.928
Sir.

584
35:59.429 --> 36:02.265
If you keep trying to force this project through,

585
36:02.348 --> 36:05.018
you could end up bringing the whole company down.

586
36:05.101 --> 36:07.479
Once we get the approval…

587
36:07.562 --> 36:08.563
I've already

588
36:09.189 --> 36:13.234
emailed Legal and Audit divisions

589
36:13.985 --> 36:15.528
about the forged resident consents,

590
36:15.612 --> 36:20.992
and the side contract you made with a subcontractor behind the company's back.

591
36:21.075 --> 36:22.368
[♪ upbeat music playing]

592
36:22.452 --> 36:23.536
Sir…

593
36:25.246 --> 36:26.831
try to see the bigger picture here.

594
36:28.041 --> 36:34.130
This land could end up becoming your grave, not a resort.

595
36:36.049 --> 36:39.594
Wait, Mr. Lee.

596
36:39.677 --> 36:42.138
I will work with you.

597
36:42.222 --> 36:44.682
I'll support you every step of the way.

598
36:44.766 --> 36:49.813
Walking out like this will mean abandoning your career.

599
36:54.025 --> 36:55.401
You can have it.

600
36:57.153 --> 36:58.196
My career.

601
37:02.408 --> 37:03.910
[music ends]

602
37:04.911 --> 37:05.912
What?

603
37:08.206 --> 37:09.207
[knocks on door]

604
37:14.462 --> 37:16.589
You never come see me.

605
37:20.343 --> 37:21.845
[sighs]

606
37:29.894 --> 37:32.814
LEE YUBIN, PROJECT DIRECTOR

607
37:35.692 --> 37:37.735
I couldn't meet your expectations.

608
37:38.736 --> 37:39.737
Sorry.

609
37:41.406 --> 37:45.201
[sighs] I love this, so I intended to give it my all…

610
37:48.788 --> 37:50.081
But this is the end of the line.

611
37:52.500 --> 37:54.002
You're joking.

612
37:55.503 --> 37:57.255
You want to blow this chance?

613
37:59.215 --> 38:01.551
I'm not blowing it. Hmm.

614
38:03.094 --> 38:04.554
I'm letting it go.

615
38:04.637 --> 38:06.514
If you are unhappy with the GM's methods,

616
38:07.515 --> 38:09.225
I can talk to the company.

617
38:09.309 --> 38:12.645
You're a valuable client.

618
38:12.729 --> 38:15.815
You put your faith in me, and you're thorough.

619
38:17.233 --> 38:19.402
Yeah. [sucks teeth]

620
38:20.486 --> 38:22.405
I may have treated you coldly…

621
38:24.908 --> 38:27.911
but I always appreciated how reliable you were.

622
38:28.995 --> 38:32.749
You should stay until this project is over. Hmm?

623
38:33.333 --> 38:35.126
Let this be your last one.

624
38:35.209 --> 38:37.462
[♪ sentimental music playing]

625
38:37.545 --> 38:39.589
Thank you for trusting me.

626
38:41.174 --> 38:42.300
But from now on,

627
38:43.009 --> 38:44.928
I'll get back on my feet on my own.

628
38:45.720 --> 38:46.846
Sia, I wish you…

629
38:48.556 --> 38:49.557
the best.

630
38:57.732 --> 38:58.733
[sighs]

631
38:59.567 --> 39:02.320
I wish he could've been mean.

632
39:05.114 --> 39:07.325
[sighs] He's the worst.

633
39:08.284 --> 39:12.205
LEE YUBIN, EXECUTIVE DIRECTOR

634
39:12.288 --> 39:13.289
[music ends]

635
39:13.373 --> 39:14.374
[sighs]

636
39:16.417 --> 39:19.337
CHARO ISLAND NOVEL STRAWBERRY VARIETY

637
39:19.420 --> 39:22.423
BRAND CONTRACT PROPOSAL

638
39:26.844 --> 39:27.845
DEAR KARIN SHIRAHAMA,

639
39:27.929 --> 39:29.305
CONGRATULATIONS ON TAKING FIRST PLACE

640
39:29.389 --> 39:30.890
AT GREEN NOVA CORPORATION FESTA.

641
39:30.974 --> 39:33.184
THESE ARE THE DETAILS OF THE SPECIAL SUPPORT PROGRAM

642
39:33.267 --> 39:34.268
AWARDED TO THE WINNER.

643
39:35.311 --> 39:36.437
[exhales]

644
39:45.446 --> 39:47.156
[in English] "Pursuant to this agreement,

645
39:47.240 --> 39:52.328
all rights relating to the crop variety's development, propagation, distribution,

646
39:52.412 --> 39:57.709
and secondary use shall be transferred to the Green Nova Corporation."

647
40:00.169 --> 40:01.629
Does this mean that

648
40:03.006 --> 40:05.258
they're only commercializing the crop seed?

649
40:05.341 --> 40:06.926
[phone buzzing]

650
40:13.558 --> 40:14.559
Karin speaking.

651
40:15.101 --> 40:18.104
Oh, Ms. Shirahama. This is Secretary Shioiri,

652
40:18.187 --> 40:22.066
calling on behalf of Executive Director Kurokawa of Green Nova Corporation.

653
40:22.650 --> 40:23.985
[Karin] Hi, thanks for calling.

654
40:24.527 --> 40:25.611
[chuckles]

655
40:25.695 --> 40:27.739
Have you had the chance to review the contract

656
40:27.822 --> 40:29.615
in the email we sent the other day?

657
40:29.699 --> 40:31.159
I'm doing it as we speak.

658
40:31.743 --> 40:33.703
Oh, that's wonderful to hear.

659
40:33.786 --> 40:35.747
You have the option to provide a digital signature.

660
40:35.830 --> 40:39.500
So I called to lend you my assistance in walking you through the signing process.

661
40:39.584 --> 40:40.835
Uh, signing?

662
40:42.211 --> 40:43.421
I still need to…

663
40:44.213 --> 40:45.757
[stammers] I'm sorry.

664
40:46.507 --> 40:48.801
I appreciate this offer and everything you've been doing,

665
40:48.885 --> 40:52.263
but I feel like the current contract

666
40:52.346 --> 40:56.100
doesn't protect my strawberries' current open-field growing method.

667
40:59.979 --> 41:02.482
Huh? What?

668
41:02.565 --> 41:06.444
Uh, Director Kurokawa informed me you'd already agreed to signing the contract.

669
41:07.028 --> 41:08.362
What?

670
41:08.446 --> 41:10.114
Director Kurokawa?

671
41:10.198 --> 41:11.532
Uh… Did…

672
41:12.575 --> 41:14.035
he really say I already signed?

673
41:15.787 --> 41:17.330
-Uh… -[sighs]

674
41:17.413 --> 41:18.414
That's, um…

675
41:18.498 --> 41:20.416
Maybe there was a miscommunication.

676
41:21.000 --> 41:23.586
I'm sorry, could you give me a little more time?

677
41:24.378 --> 41:25.421
Uh…

678
41:26.506 --> 41:28.883
Then if you don't mind, would you give me an estimate

679
41:28.966 --> 41:30.301
on when you'd have an answer?

680
41:30.384 --> 41:33.763
We were hoping to hear your reply as soon as possible.

681
41:35.098 --> 41:36.099
Absolutely.

682
41:36.182 --> 41:37.433
I'll respond soon.

683
41:38.059 --> 41:42.855
Um… as soon as I make a choice, I'll follow up with you via email.

684
41:44.273 --> 41:45.608
Thank you for your patience.

685
41:46.859 --> 41:47.860
Goodbye, sir.

686
41:50.780 --> 41:51.823
[sighs]

687
41:57.161 --> 42:00.164
[♪ ominous music playing]

688
42:11.300 --> 42:12.301
[music ends]

689
42:15.012 --> 42:17.515
[♪ gentle music playing]

690
42:20.101 --> 42:21.269
[Karin sighs]

691
42:23.271 --> 42:26.190
[Kurokawa] What do you think about creating a brand for your strawberries?

692
42:26.274 --> 42:27.817
Creating a brand, sir?

693
42:28.401 --> 42:29.986
Nationwide distribution.

694
42:30.069 --> 42:32.071
We could send your berries throughout Japan.

695
42:33.322 --> 42:36.909
Don't you want more people to experience your produce?

696
42:44.125 --> 42:45.585
[voice, in distance] Hey, boss!

697
42:50.339 --> 42:52.049
Hey, boss!

698
42:53.885 --> 42:55.887
[♪ upbeat rock music playing]

699
42:55.970 --> 42:58.014
[footsteps echoing]

700
43:38.346 --> 43:39.347
[groans]

701
43:46.854 --> 43:47.855
Karin.

702
43:50.149 --> 43:51.150
I'm home.

703
43:52.610 --> 43:53.945
Welcome back.

704
44:17.510 --> 44:19.804
MERRY BERRY LOVE

705
44:19.887 --> 44:20.888
NEXT EPISODE

706
44:20.972 --> 44:22.515
I'm back to square one.

707
44:22.598 --> 44:24.892
-[Karin] It's a welcome party for you. -Cheers!

708
44:25.851 --> 44:29.105
[Kurokawa] Of course… No wonder he's such an eyesore.
